input arrays reversed: sec 7.4: the root's seq-2 twin of its succession is reachable only from its seq-3 entry, which the root anchors in the second of its handing off; the record is one at which the root has retired, DISCARDED, yet timeliness reads that second by position: the seq-2 twin sits at the retiring seq and is timely, a fork with the succession, while the seq-3 entry above it stays RETIRED.
